// ─── What Sam has agreed to ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// A contract is a promise of flows to come: with whom, how much, how often,
// and what for.
// - The journal records each time a contract is kept, in one line, plus what
//   differed that time.
// - The forecast runs every contract forward.
// - `check` notices when one is not kept, such as a rent that never came or
//   a bill missing from a statement.
// - What a contract says about its flows (a share, a covered
//   period, a loan's interest) applies to every one of them without being
//   written again.

/// The job: 110,400 USD a year, paid on the 15th and the last day of the
/// month. Each paystub is restated in the journal, since its amounts move.
contract job with lumen
  4_600 USD twice monthly on 15, last into checking   // gross; checking takes what is left
  retirement   6%                          // ▸ pre-tax deferral: into a 401k, from wages
  blue-shield  184.20 USD #premium         // ▸ pre-tax (§125): out of wages and payroll tax
  also lumen -> retirement 50% of ([retirement] up to 6% of amount) #match
                                           // ▸ Lumen adds 138.00 to each paycheck's 276.00

/// The flat. Its second bedroom, 120 of its 1,000 square feet, is the studio's
/// office. Greystar bills a share of the building's water each quarter.
contract flat with greystar
  2_900 USD monthly on 1 from checking     // ▸ rent: greystar is a landlord
  area 1_000 SQFT                          // its whole area, used to measure the studio's share
  share 120 SQFT for studio                // ▸ 12%: 348.00 of each rent is the studio's
  input water USD                          // the building's water bill, on the months it comes
  + 12% of water #utilities
  until 2026-08-31

contract phone with mint
  45 USD monthly on 8 from visa            // ▸ phone: mint is a phone company
  share 60% for studio                     // ▸ 27.00 of each bill is the studio's

contract figma with figma
  15 USD monthly on 3 from visa
  share 100% for studio

contract netflix with netflix
  15.49 USD monthly on 22 from visa

contract gym with equinox
  240 USD monthly on 1 from visa

/// The condo's loan: 320,000 USD at 5.875% over thirty years. How much of
/// each payment is interest, and how much is principal, follows from these
/// terms. Nobody splits a payment by hand, and `check` compares the balance
/// with the statements.
contract mortgage with rocket
  loan 320_000 USD on 2024-02-20 at 5.875% over 30y for condo
  monthly on 1 from checking               // ▸ 1,892.92: the payment follows from the loan
  also -> escrow 410 USD #escrow           // property tax and insurance, with each payment

/// Dana's lease on the condo, with a deposit held for her.
contract lease with dana
  2_350 USD monthly on 1 into checking #rent of condo
  deposit 2_350 USD                        // ▸ held for dana: not Sam's to spend, owed back at the end
  grace 3d                                 // her February payment was two days late; March's is four days late
  from 2025-07-01
  until 2026-06-30

contract condo-insurance with state-farm
  1_140 USD yearly on 03-01 from checking #insurance of condo
  covers the year                          // ▸ recognized at 95.00 a month

/// A standing order: 500 USD of VTI on the 20th.
contract vti-monthly with fidelity
  buy VTI for 500 USD monthly on 20 from checking
